          "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Pm2Mg2Pd2 (PmMgPd) crystallizes in the hexagonal system with space group P6_3/mmc (No. 194) and a unit cell containing 6 atoms distributed over 3 independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis identifies close-packed-like local arrangements for all three elements: Mg and Pd each have 12 geometric neighbors per center atom, while Pm also has 12 neighbors, with neighbor distances spanning 3.03–3.44 Å. The periodic geometric neighbor graph forms a single 3-dimensional component containing all 6 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing relations reveal that Mg–Pm and Pd–Pd 12-vertex coordination polyhedra exhibit corner-, edge-, and face-sharing patterns.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
